[00:00.000 --> 00:03.360]  These are the three laws of fast-spitting gyroscopes.
[00:03.360 --> 00:06.400]  First of all, a fast-spitting gyroscope
[00:06.400 --> 00:11.520]  likes to stay in one place and won't rotate or process.
[00:14.880 --> 00:19.520]  Secondly, when a spinning gyroscope feels the downward force of gravity,
[00:19.520 --> 00:24.400]  it will always spin or process in the same direction that its server disk is spinning.
[00:25.280 --> 00:29.840]  And that procession will cancel the force of gravity that's pulling downward.
[00:30.400 --> 00:34.080]  A spinning gyroscope will rotate or process slowly
[00:34.080 --> 00:37.680]  so as to cancel the force of gravity which was applied to it.
[00:38.320 --> 00:46.000]  As the spin of its inner disk slows down, so does its cancelling anti-gravity effect.
[00:53.680 --> 00:57.760]  And eventually the weight all goes down to the bottom again.
[00:57.760 --> 01:05.680]  For the third law, most interestingly, when that gyroscope is rotating or processing slowly
[01:05.680 --> 01:10.240]  to cancel the effect of gravity, if we make it just process a little bit faster,
[01:10.240 --> 01:15.840]  it's like a gear and now we get an anti-gravity effect not just cancelling.
[01:27.760 --> 01:32.400]  It needs to be theoretically and experimentally studied further.
[01:32.400 --> 01:34.800]  You'll be very fruitful results.
[01:35.280 --> 01:41.980] 
   Word count: ~169 words

