[00:00.000 --> 00:05.000]  Today we're going to study why a spinning gyroscope lifts up against gravity.
[00:05.000 --> 00:09.000]  First we give it a little spin and then we give it a nudge from the side.
[00:09.000 --> 00:14.000]  You can see it lifts up and spins quite nicely.
[00:14.000 --> 00:16.000]  So why is that exactly?
[00:16.000 --> 00:21.000]  The physics is much more deep and mysterious than you could possibly imagine.
[00:22.000 --> 00:28.000]  First thing we have to realize is that you just can't push it up directly without spin.
[00:28.000 --> 00:33.000]  It doesn't want to move straight up in a vertical direction no matter how we push it.
[00:33.000 --> 00:38.000]  If there's no spin we can push it around all we want.
[00:38.000 --> 00:43.000]  Strangely enough we require an outside force to make it lift up.
[00:43.000 --> 00:50.000]  When the disk is spinning see our way from us and we touch it sideways you can see the blue side lifts up.
[00:50.000 --> 00:57.000]  When the disk is spinning tortoise we touch it sideways you can see the red side lifts up.
[00:57.000 --> 01:02.000]  The way from us the blue side lifts up.
[01:02.000 --> 01:06.000]  Tortoise the red side lifts up.
[01:06.000 --> 01:08.000]  That's very strange isn't it?
[01:08.000 --> 01:10.000]  Let's analyze it further.
[01:10.000 --> 01:19.000]  Now if the central disk is not spinning and we give it a horizontal force it just spins in the same plane and doesn't lift up at all.
[01:19.000 --> 01:24.000]  So it has to do something with the central disk spinning to change the behavior.
[01:25.000 --> 01:39.000]  However when the disk is spinning and we apply a horizontal torque then that gets converted to a rotation that way or that way in a vertical direction which gives the lifting anti-gravity force of a gyroscope.
[01:39.000 --> 01:42.000]  Let's look at it one more time.
[01:42.000 --> 01:53.000]  This case our horizontal rotation gets shifted to a vertical rotation about an axis 90 degrees away from where the force was applied.
[01:53.000 --> 02:02.000]  And that's the very principle of how gyroscopes lift up when they get increased torque.
