[00:00.500 --> 00:04.500]  I'm working today to build a small model for a flying saucer.
[00:04.500 --> 00:08.500]  We start with one, two, three, three-phase wire coils.
[00:08.500 --> 00:13.500]  There's a stainless steel bowl here with a stainless steel dowel of five millimeters,
[00:13.500 --> 00:16.000]  40 millimeter magnet inside.
[00:16.000 --> 00:19.700]  When we turn on the three-phase power, it'll spin and lift up.
[00:19.700 --> 00:24.500]  Now what I want to do first, I want to put a top on the flying saucer like this.
[00:24.500 --> 00:26.900]  So now it looks like a saucer.
[00:30.000 --> 00:33.500]  Start with the magnet spinning inside.
[00:33.500 --> 00:37.000]  Ten hertz and let's see what happens.
[00:37.000 --> 00:40.000]  Twenty hertz.
[00:40.000 --> 00:45.000]  Twenty five hertz.
[00:46.000 --> 00:52.000]  There we go.
[00:52.000 --> 01:01.000]  Lift up.
[01:01.000 --> 01:14.000]  You can see the same thing without the bowl being on top.
[01:14.000 --> 01:21.000]  The magnet lifts up.
[01:21.000 --> 01:25.000]  Considerable force.
[01:25.000 --> 01:26.000]  So that's our first model.
[01:26.000 --> 01:28.000]  We're going to see how far we can go from there.
[01:28.000 --> 01:31.000]  Thank you to the stars.
