[00:00.000 --> 00:07.920]  The coordinates 49.27 north and 11.5 east fall inside a historically active region
[00:07.920 --> 00:12.800]  of southern Germany tied to unexplained aerial events, cold war intelligence and
[00:12.800 --> 00:14.760]  recurring crop formations.
[00:14.760 --> 00:21.400]  The location sits within the same corridor as the 1561 Nuremberg Mass Sighting.
[00:21.400 --> 00:26.340]  Now this mass sighting was a mass daylight event witnessed by hundreds of residents
[00:26.340 --> 00:30.460]  of Nuremberg on the morning of April 14, 1561.
[00:30.460 --> 00:36.420]  At dawn, people reported seeing dozens of strange objects in the sky described as spheres,
[00:36.420 --> 00:42.700]  cylinders, crosses and rod shaped forms moving rapidly and appearing to collide as if
[00:42.700 --> 00:45.580]  engaged in aerial battle.
[00:45.580 --> 00:49.620]  Some of the objects were said to fall toward the ground at a time of city, after which a
[00:49.620 --> 00:55.260]  large, black, spear or arrow-shaped object reportedly appeared overhead.
[00:55.260 --> 01:01.700]  The event was recorded in a woodcut and pamphlet by Hans Glazer who framed it as a frightening
[01:01.700 --> 01:06.180]  sign from the heavens.
   Word count: ~147 words

